Initialise the restore node of a surface blob (series with a restore list: 7.3+).

virtio_gpu_vram_init() builds the object behind VIRTGPU_LIMINA_SURFACE_CREATE without
virtio_gpu_vram_create()'s INIT_LIST_HEAD. From 7.3 on, virtio_gpu_vram_free() list_del_init()s
every created blob's restore_node, so freeing a surface tripped list_debug's BUG and wedged the
freeing task in D state: gnome-shell on the Metal transport never reached its desktop.
Applied only where virtgpu_drv.h has restore_node; older series have no such field.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
@@ -212,6 +212,8 @@
 
 	obj = &vram->base.base.base;
 	obj->funcs = &virtio_gpu_vram_funcs;
+
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&vram->base.restore_node);
 
 	params->size = PAGE_ALIGN(params->size);
 	drm_gem_private_object_init(vgdev->ddev, obj, params->size);
